    [bold]KOTAHI RULEBOOK[/bold]

     The deck

    108 cards: 25 in each of four colours (blue, red, green, yellow) plus 8 black ones.
    Every colour holds one zero, two of each number from 1 to 9, and two each of Draw Two,
    Reverse and Skip. The black cards are four Wilds and four Wild Draw Fours.

     Setup

    Take the deck out of the box and shuffle it thoroughly.
    Deal 7 cards to every player; hold them so no one else sees their faces.
    Put the rest face down in a stack — that is the draw pile.
    Turn its top card over and set it beside the pile: that starts the discard pile.

     Playing

    Play passes around the circle. On your turn play one card onto the discard pile that matches
    the top card by colour or by number (or by type — a Skip goes onto a Skip).
    A black card may be played at any time, on top of anything.
    If nothing matches, draw one card from the draw pile. If it fits you may play it at once;
    otherwise your turn ends.

     Special cards

    [bold]Draw Two[/bold] — the next player draws two cards and loses their turn.
    [bold]Reverse[/bold] — play turns around. With two players it acts as a Skip: you go again.
    [bold]Skip[/bold] — the next player loses their turn.
    [bold]Wild[/bold] (black) — whoever plays it names any colour out loud; play continues in that colour.
    [bold]Wild Draw Four[/bold] (black) — the same, and the next player draws four cards and loses
    their turn. By convention you may only play it when you hold no card of the current colour.

     The call

    The moment a turn leaves you with [bold]one[/bold] card, shout "Kotahi!" at once.
    Forget, and get caught before the next player moves, and you draw two cards as a penalty.

     Ending the game

    The round ends when someone plays their last card — that player wins.
    If the draw pile runs out, set the top discard aside, shuffle the rest of the discards,
    and they become the new draw pile.
